From 57a0cdc9411ad22a81e0c064b789652c06750928 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:14:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix redundant month header, real report title, right-leaning
 toolbar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Dropped "{month} Timeline" down to just "Timeline" in the left rail
   header — the month is already shown once, in the toolbar above (with
   its own prev/next/Today nav), repeating it there was pure duplication.

2. "Executive Audit Report" was an 11px uppercase label, not a title,
   for what is actually the centerpiece content of the page. Promoted
   to a real h2 at title weight/size, matching the verdict banner's
   register instead of looking like a small section tag.

3. Found the actual cause of content "leaning right" in the embedded
   view: ViewSwitcher had a hardcoded ml-auto, correct when there's a
   search box to its left (standalone run page) but wrong when embedded
   here — the search box is hidden in embedded mode, so ml-auto had
   nothing to balance and just yanked the Calendar/List toggle to the
   far right with a large empty gap in front of it. Now ml-auto only
   applies when not embedded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
